      "body": "## Motivation\n\nEnabling the AdaLN sidecar cache on FastH3 (`--minimax-h3-adaln-cache-path`) always fails, even though FastH3 is a supported pipeline:\n\n- `FastH3PipelineConfig.validate_server_args` raises on any explicit `--model-variant` (FastH3 ships a single t2va-distilled partition, so the flag does not apply).\n- The sidecar branch in `TransformerLoader` required `model_variant in (\"fl2va\", \"ref2va\")` and raised `MiniMax H3 AdaLN cache requires --model-variant fl2va or ref2va` otherwise.\n\nWith FastH3 the variant is therefore always `None`, so the two checks deadlock the only supported FastH3 + sidecar path.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `_resolve_minimax_h3_adaln_variant(model_variant)`: an unset variant now falls back to `fl2va`, the same default the base `MiniMaxH3PipelineConfig` already selects when `--model-variant` is omitted. Unsupported values still raise the existing error.\n- Use it in the sidecar branch instead of the inline `in (\"fl2va\", \"ref2va\")` check.\n- Add unit tests covering the three boundary cases (unset -> `fl2va`, supported passthrough, unsupported rejection) to the existing `test_minimax_h3_adaln_cache.py`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValidated end to end on a single A100-SXM4-80GB (FastH3 4-step, 1344x768, 5 s, Triton VSA fallback). Output is **bit-exact** with the pre-patch baseline (`MD5 60e0244b...` identical), so the fix only unblocks the path without changing numerics.\n\n`python -m pytest python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_minimax_h3_adaln_cache.py` -> 26 passed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nSame prompt/seed/resolution/steps, VAE-resident + layerwise offload of `dit text_encoder`:\n\n| run | e2e (s) | peak VRAM (MB) | DiT host pinned (GiB) | output MD5 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| baseline (no sidecar) | 84.96 | 20210 | 65.15 | 60e0244b... |\n| + AdaLN sidecar | 85.67 (+0.8%, noise) | 19236 (-0.97 GiB) | 40.91 (-24.24) | 60e0244b... bit-exact |\n\nThe 24.2 GiB of `adaln_proj` weights no longer need to be re-streamed per request; the saving is hidden behind compute for this single-request, compute-bound case, so wall time is unchanged while VRAM and host pinned memory drop.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to Write documentations.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to Test the accuracy and Benchmark the speed.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38114951984](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114951984)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38114951760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114951760)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38114951738](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38114951738)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
